The idea started out in my head. Apply a magic marker to oneself and draw 
a design. The tattoo would confer some ability or intrinsic until the 
tattoo was removed (attacking an acidic monster and getting splashed, 
rust trap or falling into water or bathing in a fountain while quaffing, 
etc) from one's person.
The tattoo could be made permanent by reading a scroll of enchant armor 
when wearing nothing at all.
Of course where would one get the ideas for tattoos? Folks would just 
want to write "Elbereth" on their foreheads or draw a heart with "MOM" in 
the middle. There would be special kinds of scrolls which would have 
diagrams or designs for the player to use.

Various tattoos could be:

Dragon tattoo: breathe fire if the character has enough magic points
Cherry blossom tattoo: d6+1 charisma boost to racial maximum
Mountain tattoo: disintegration resistance
Falcon tattoo: speed boost
Gnat tattoo: AC lowered by d6+1

and so on and so forth.

This could be interesting for gameplay to confer intrinsics on players 
who wouldn't normally get them (vegetarian conduct, etc) or that person 
just simply hasn't had the chance to get such an intrinsic because the 
RNG decided there weren't any black dragons. There would be an extra 
challenge to the game coming from a trade-off when one acquires the 
tattoo. For example, the cherry blossom tattoo would move points from 
one's constitution to charisma considering the less physical lifestyle 
one would have with better people skills.

Of course instead of this nonsense, there could be a new shopkeeper found 
in Minetown (50% chance) who's a tattoo artist and will gladly give 
someone the appropriate tattoo for 400 zorkmids x XP level. Only one 
tattoo per customer since I would see these tattoos as covering most if 
not all of the body, not leaving much room for another.

Thank you for humoring me.

